course: dictionary
lesson: 11474
title: A small airfield called an aerodrome
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An aerodrome is a small airfield where planes take off and land. It does not have a big airport building. «The little aerodrome had just one runway and a small wooden hut.» The words small, one runway and a hut are your clues: an aerodrome is a small place for planes.
explain: Look at the words around a new word to work out its meaning. «Dad's plane took off from the aerodrome at dawn.» Took off and dawn tell you that planes leave from there early in the morning. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Dad's plane took off from the small airfield at dawn." It still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Some words are old-fashioned. «In the old war films, pilots ran from the aerodrome to their planes.» The old films show that this word is from long ago, when planes were new. Today many people would say airfield or airport instead.
explain: Words can change from place to place. People in the UK, Australia and New Zealand use aerodrome for a small local airfield. In the USA, people say «airfield» or «airport». When you are not sure, a dictionary will tell you what a word means.
fact: An aerodrome is a small airfield where planes take off and land.
fact: An aerodrome does not have a big airport building.
fact: «Aerodrome» is an old-fashioned word, used mostly in the UK and Australia.
fact: In the USA, people say «airfield» or «airport» for this kind of place.
fact: Context clues, such as small, runway or took off, can help you work out what aerodrome means.
exercise: «The little aerodrome had just one runway and a small wooden hut.» What is an aerodrome? | A place where ships are repaired | A kind of very big aeroplane | *A small airfield where planes take off and land | A huge airport with shops and cafés
exercise: Ella's first flying lesson was at the local aerodrome, not at a big airport. What does this tell you? | *The aerodrome is smaller than a big airport | The aerodrome is a kind of boat | The aerodrome is under the sea | The aerodrome is bigger than a big airport
exercise: «Dad's plane took off from the aerodrome at dawn.» Find and copy one word that tells you when the plane left. | Dad's | plane | *dawn | aerodrome
test: «Pilots ran from the aerodrome to their planes in the old war films.» What does aerodrome mean? | *A small airfield where planes take off and land | A large shop at an airport | A hangar full of old cars | A school for pilots
test: A British child says, «We'll walk to the aerodrome to watch the planes.» An American child would more likely say what? | harbour | *airfield | aerodrome | station
exam: Sam reads, «The aerodrome was quiet, with one hut and a windsock.» Which clues help you work out what aerodrome means? | There are no clues, so you cannot guess | The word windsock shows it is a school | The word quiet shows it is a shop | *The words quiet, one hut and windsock show a small place for planes
